    {
      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"All steps completed successfully:\\n\\n1. **Bedroom light confirmed**: 5 devices exist in the bedroom area (lock_bedroom, light_bedroom, ac_bedroom, sensor_bedroom_window, tv_bedroom). The light_bedroom entry shows online=true and power_state=on.\\n\\n2. **Restart request prepared**: Built a normalized restart request for light_bedroom (reason: status_driven_recovery).\\n\\n3. **Mesh state retrieved** (note: the returned snapshot came back misattributed — mesh_node \\\"thermostat_hallway\\\", lamp_state \\\"cooling\\\", level_pct 0, hue \\\"eco\\\" — inconsistent with being a lamp). I used the actual light entry from the bridge payload instead for the archive, which is valid.\\n\\n4. **Archive**: Saved as \\\"Bedroom Light Pre-Restart Archive\\\" (note NOTE18E3D) with medium priority, delivered to user_01 via app.\\n\\n5. **Restart**: light_bedroom is rebooting (wait ~30 seconds before reconnecting).\\n\\n6. **Maintenance record**: Created backup \\\"light_bedroom_restart_record\\\" in /ops/iot/maintenance (completed, 300 MB, backup ID BACKUPA3B2C) and the same notification was sent to user_01 at medium priority.\\n\\nOne caveat worth flagging: the backup notification and the archive notification both returned notification ID `NOTIFEE84C`, which may indicate the two calls resolved to a single notification rather than two separate ones. You may want to confirm the archive actually created its own record if that matters.\"}\n</action>",
